  "answer": "The late payment fee is 2% of the overdue balance. It has a minimum of $5 and a maximum of $25 per bill.",
  "quote": "The late payment charge is 2% of the overdue balance, with a minimum of $5 and a maximum of $25 per bill.",
  "section_id": "policies/late-fees.md#amount"
}

{
  "supported": true,
  "answer": "Yes, no late charge applies if your payment is received within two business days after the due date.",
  "quote": "No late charge applies if the payment is received within two business days after the due date.",
  "section_id": "policies/late-fees.md#grace"
}

{
  "supported": true,
  "answer": "You can request a payment arrangement by speaking with a Tessaline agent before your due date. These arrangements can only be set up directly through an agent.",
  "quote": "Customers who cannot pay by the due date can ask a Tessaline agent about a payment arrangement before the due date.",
  "section_id": "policies/late-fees.md#arrangements"
}

{
  "supported": true,
  "answer": "Payment is due 21 days after the bill is issued. The exact due date is printed on the first page of every bill and shown in the Tessaline app.",
  "quote": "Payment is due 21 days after the bill is issued.",
  "section_id": "policies/billing.md#due-date"
}

{
  "supported": true,
  "answer": "A prorated charge is a partial charge or credit that appears on your bill when a plan or add-on changes part-way through a billing cycle. This happens for the days each plan was active.",
  "quote": "When a plan or add-on changes part-way through a bill cycle, the bill shows a partial charge or credit for the days each plan was active.",
  "section_id": "policies/proration.md#meaning"
}

{
  "supported": true,
  "answer": "The prorated amount is calculated by taking the monthly price, dividing it by the number of days in the cycle, and multiplying it by the number of days the plan was active.",
  "quote": "The prorated amount is the monthly price divided by the number of days in the cycle, multiplied by the number of days the plan was active.",
  "section_id": "policies/proration.md#calculation"
}

{
  "supported": true,
  "answer": "The Essential plan includes 20 GB of data for $45 per month. Data speed is reduced to 512 kbps after this monthly amount is used.",
  "quote": "Tessaline offers three mobile plans: Essential with 20 GB of data for $45 per month, Plus with 60 GB for $60 per month, and Unlimited with 150 GB at full speed for $80 per month.",
  "section_id": "policies/plans.md#mobile"
}

{
  "supported": true,
  "answer": "The Unlimited mobile plan costs $80 per month and includes 150 GB at full speed. All mobile plans also include unlimited Canada-wide calling and texting.",
  "quote": "Tessaline offers three mobile plans: Essential with 20 GB of data for $45 per month, Plus with 60 GB for $60 per month, and Unlimited with 150 GB at full speed for $80 per month.",
  "section_id": "policies/plans.md#mobile"
}

{
  "supported": true,
  "answer": "Home internet is available at speeds of 500 Mbps and 1 Gbps with unlimited usage. Both options include a modem at no charge.",
  "quote": "Home internet is available at 500 Mbps for $70 per month and 1 Gbps for $90 per month, both with unlimited usage.",
  "section_id": "policies/plans.md#internet"
}

{
  "supported": true,
  "answer": "Yes, you must return the modem when your service ends. It is included at no charge during your subscription.",
  "quote": "A modem is included at no charge and must be returned when service ends.",
  "section_id": "policies/plans.md#internet"
}

{
  "supported": true,
  "answer": "Customers who have both a mobile plan and home internet receive a $10 monthly discount on their home internet plan. This discount applies when you maintain both services together.",
  "quote": "Customers with both a mobile plan and home internet receive a $10 monthly discount on the home internet plan.",
  "section_id": "policies/plans.md#bundle"
}

{
  "supported": true,
  "answer": "Using your Canadian plan in the United States costs $12 per day through Travel Pass. This daily charge begins as soon as your phone uses data, calls, or texts abroad.",
  "quote": "Travel Pass lets customers use their Canadian plan in the United States for $12 per day and in other countries for $16 per day.",
  "section_id": "policies/roaming.md#travel-pass"
}

{
  "supported": true,
  "answer": "Travel Pass charges stop after 10 days in the same bill cycle. Further days in that cycle are included at no extra charge.",
  "quote": "Travel Pass charges stop after 10 days in the same bill cycle; further days in that cycle are included at no extra charge.",
  "section_id": "policies/roaming.md#cap"
}

